//
// Node.js version (from node -v):
//
// npm version (from npm -v):
//
// Is the Node.js version 20 or higher?

problems.solution:
**A model answer.** Your numbers will be different, which is expected.

```ts
// Problem 1: my Node.js and npm versions
//
// Node.js version (from node -v): v22.12.0
//
// npm version (from npm -v): 10.9.0
//
// Is the Node.js version 20 or higher? Yes, it is 22.
```

**What makes a good answer** is that both numbers come from your own terminal. When a test behaves differently on two computers, the Node.js version is one of the first things to compare. If your version is lower than 20, install the LTS version from https://nodejs.org before Day 3.

